      "text": "Qus 1 -> Why only we can return only one parent in JSX",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Qus 1 -> Why only we can return only one parent in JSX",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5rkQv5XLD-dn9A_vhLbuG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1386.3783845411454,
      "y": 82860.79091594061,
      "width": 1001,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1794664246,
      "version": 195,
      "versionNonce": 39010614,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780363161292,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Because we can't return more that 1 object, and each tag in HTML in DOM is a object, if we \nwant to return then inside one parent we can return multiple objects.\n\nHome.js",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Because we can't return more that 1 object, and each tag in HTML in DOM is a object, if we \nwant to return then inside one parent we can return multiple objects.\n\nHome.js",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0SL7ZObslDfaAvrOOq6xN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1422.3236970411454,
      "y": 82970.64247844061,
      "width": 968,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1981603818,
      "version": 253,
      "versionNonce": 1372852906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780363291492,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "import React from \"react\";\n\nconst Home = () => {\n    return (\n        <div>\n            <h1>Home Page</h1>\n            <h1>Home Page1</h1>\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;\n\n\n# error\nconst Home = () => {\n    return (\n            <h1>Home Page</h1>\n            <h1>Home Page1</h1>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;\n\n\n# No error but here we will get last element, like Js function\nconst Home = () => {\n    return (\n            <h1>Home Page</h1>,\n            <h1>Home Page1</h1>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;\n\n\nHence HTML elements are objects, and we can't return more than one object in Javascript.\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "import React from \"react\";\n\nconst Home = () => {\n    return (\n        <div>\n            <h1>Home Page</h1>\n            <h1>Home Page1</h1>\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;\n\n\n# error\nconst Home = () => {\n    return (\n            <h1>Home Page</h1>\n            <h1>Home Page1</h1>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;\n\n\n# No error but here we will get last element, like Js function\nconst Home = () => {\n    return (\n            <h1>Home Page</h1>,\n            <h1>Home Page1</h1>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;\n\n\nHence HTML elements are objects, and we can't return more than one object in Javascript.\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
