      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Qus 14 What is controlled components?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JypSjIRluI3ncpOGl5G_j",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1354.5893220411454,
      "y": 88481.94716594061,
      "width": 1067,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bra",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 191855722,
      "version": 309,
      "versionNonce": 1413890294,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780368463129,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "whenever we have form and input fields inside component, and we are controlling these inputs with\nthe help of states then we see that component is controlled component.\n\nand when we get input fields directly from DOM then we see that it is a uncontrolled component.\n\nimport React from \"react\";\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\n\nconst Home = () => {\n    const [name, setName] = useState('');\n    return (\n        <div>\n            <h1>Controlled Component</h1>\n            <form action='' method='get'>\n                <input type = \"text\" \n                value = {name}\n                placeholder=\"Enter Name\" onChange={(event)=> setName(event.target.value)}/>\n                <button>Submit</button>\n\n            </form>\n            <h1>{name}</h1>\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "whenever we have form and input fields inside component, and we are controlling these inputs with\nthe help of states then we see that component is controlled component.\n\nand when we get input fields directly from DOM then we see that it is a uncontrolled component.\n\nimport React from \"react\";\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\n\nconst Home = () => {\n    const [name, setName] = useState('');\n    return (\n        <div>\n            <h1>Controlled Component</h1>\n            <form action='' method='get'>\n                <input type = \"text\" \n                value = {name}\n                placeholder=\"Enter Name\" onChange={(event)=> setName(event.target.value)}/>\n                <button>Submit</button>\n\n            </form>\n            <h1>{name}</h1>\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\nexport default Home;",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
